<p>Well, I'll point out reasons to these things as best I can.</p>
<ol>
<li>Since the foundation is above every law, they could just tell them to leave, assuming they didn't already make arrangements for these outbreaks, which they have.</li>
<li>only if they touch the paint. you could burn a building without touching it.</li>
<li>SCP-274 made the rooms into a digestive track. Every room, barring the first one you walk into, is an organ.</li>
<li>They 'act' as antibodies. It's another means of disposal. Since <em>they</em> can't actually eat them (highly complex organism vs single celled), they incapacitate them, clean them to prevent contamination, and then chuck them into something that can eat them. As for waste, they are made into SCP-274, and another SCP-274-2.</li>
</ol>
<p>you're right on it needing work though&#8230; I just don't know where to go with it.</p>
<p>edit: AM I THE ONLY ONE?! Also, you could walk past it, and happen to get it on you, you could have realized that the graffiti has been wet for ages, and touched it out of curiosity, or it could have gotten on your house while you were away, so you tried to paint over it, failing miserably. No wet paint signs too, so people who lean against walls.</p>

